bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T04:03:35-07:00","id":1397050,"title":"","content":"To pitch in with my opinion: while Mr. &amp; Mrs. Smith definitely could work as a framework for Angel/Demon couples, I see that movie is much more fitting for a romantic relationship between a pair of Demon agents who are unaware that they work for separate agencies- it allows for more a more comedic and slightly more humanistic tone.<br /> <br /> Also, I\u2019m tickled pink that people found a renewed interest in this subject; it\u2019s one of my more favorite topics to ponder on <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T06:13:04-07:00","id":1397073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demo